Now, the next part is about how many shelves he needs. Each shelf can fit 4 books. So I need to divide the number of books he has by the number of books per shelf. That would be 36 divided by 4. Let me do that division. 36 divided by 4 is 9. So he needs 9 shelves. Wait, but let me double-check. If each shelf holds 4 books, then 9 shelves would hold 9 times 4, which is 36. That matches the number of books he has. So that seems right. 

